winewayland: a fullscreen window of an emulated display mode keeps its aspect ratio

win32u draws an emulated mode's fullscreen window (a 640x480 game on a 1920x1080 monitor) scaled at one
ratio for both axes into its window rect, (240,0)-(1680,1080), and stretches its visible rect over the
whole monitor. The driver presented the visible rect: the window's 1536-wide buffer (1440 drawn, rounded
up to 128) as the viewport's source, scaled to 1920 — the picture 1800 px wide, its right part cut off.
The driver now presents the window rect when it lies inside the visible one: the 1440x1080 picture,
which the compositor centers on the output (xdg_toplevel.set_fullscreen; X547's server: patches/
wayland_server/...-fullscreen-center.patch).

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c	2026-10-22 08:57:33.324853406 +0200
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c	2026-10-22 08:57:33.332814013 +0200
@@ -139,6 +139,17 @@
     DWORD style;
 
     conf->rect = data->rects.visible;
+    /* A fullscreen window of an emulated display mode keeps its aspect ratio:
+     * win32u stretches its visible rect over the whole monitor, but draws its
+     * contents scaled into its window rect, inside the visible one. Present
+     * the window rect, which the compositor centers on the output. */
+    if (data->is_fullscreen && !EqualRect(&data->rects.window, &data->rects.visible))
+    {
+        RECT inside;
+        if (intersect_rect(&inside, &data->rects.window, &data->rects.visible) &&
+            EqualRect(&inside, &data->rects.window))
+            conf->rect = data->rects.window;
+    }
     style = NtUserGetWindowLongW(data->hwnd, GWL_STYLE);
 
     TRACE("window=%s style=%#x\n", wine_dbgstr_rect(&conf->rect), style);
